---
import { siteUrl } from '../../utils/site';
import Definition from '../../layouts/Definition.astro';
---

<Definition title="Launch to Title" section="Journey">
  <div slot="preview" class="notice">
    <p>Phantasy Star Zero fan remake</p>
    <p>Unofficial. Not affiliated with or endorsed by SEGA.<br />Phantasy Star Zero and its original content © SEGA.</p>
    <p>Follow @wagieweeb on X for updates.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Scope and identity</h2>
  <p>Splash covers the entire player experience from launching the application to reaching the title: OS icon and name, engine splash, asset preparation, first-run controls, and transitions. Owner direction, 2026-10-10: a fan adaptation bringing PSZ's gameplay and story closer to PSO's style, rather than only a one-to-one engine port.</p>
  <p>The player-facing application name remains <strong>PSZ Godot</strong> for now. Every exported platform MUST use the same Rappy identity, with suitable launcher masks and sizes. Android package and macOS bundle identifiers MUST remain stable.</p>

  <h2>Boot notice</h2>
  <p>The native engine splash MUST be black with centered white text using the wording shown above. It MUST preserve aspect ratio, fit smaller and wider displays, and have no anniversary logo, animation, acknowledgement button, or minimum display time. The bootstrap MUST retain the same image while preparing a cached pack so the patch screen does not flash on repeat launches.</p>

  <h2>Startup paths</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Verified, unchanged pack:</strong> validate its local receipt and mount immediately. No HTTP client initialization, network request, full hash scan, download UI, or artificial hold.</li>
    <li><strong>Existing pack without a valid receipt:</strong> verify once, then save a receipt after a successful mount. Verification MUST yield on a time budget, not once per MiB, so frame rate does not dictate startup duration.</li>
    <li><strong>Missing, changed, or corrupt required pack:</strong> show the <a href={siteUrl('/journey/download')}>asset download screen</a>, verify the full hash, and mount before proceeding.</li>
    <li><strong>Controls:</strong> show setup only when no saved input configuration exists; otherwise enter the title directly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The title depends on resources inside the required pack. This iteration does not load an old pack with a new executable or add a remote update service. A small bottom-right title indicator is reserved for real future background work; no idle or simulated loader is shown.</p>

  <h2>Acceptance and evidence</h2>
  <p>Unit tests MUST cover receipt invalidation (hash, size, modification time, missing or malformed receipt) and verification failure. A runtime startup probe MUST cover first download, repeat cached launch, migration from an unreceipted cache, and corrupt-cache recovery. Visual review MUST cover 640×360, 1280×720, 1920×1080, 4:3 and ultrawide, plus launcher icons on exported platforms. Passing automated checks does not substitute for owner playtesting or raise scorecard grades.</p>
</Definition>

<style>
  .notice { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; background: #000; color: #fff; text-align: center; padding: 8%; box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
  .notice p { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(12px, 1.6vw, 24px); line-height: 1.6; }
  .notice p:first-child { font-size: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 32px); }
</style>
